 "verdict": "confirmed",
 "derivation": "French globule is not a popular descendant of globus but a learned formation taken from Latin globulus, the regular diminutive of globus, into scientific French of the 16th-17th c. (Klein: 'globule, n. — F., fr. L. globulus, \"a little ball\", dimin. of globus'). Ernout-Meillet list globulus among the dérivés of globus. So the chart's Latin→French arrow is right in substance; only the intermediate globulus is left implicit.",
